    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0553" n="541" xml:id="pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.50/13</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the
                        Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Alling</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-17">June 17, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Alling</hi>: I received this morning a visit
                    from Rabbi Wise and some of his colleagues. Dr. Wise informed me that there were
                    news reports alleging that the Prime Minister of Iraq<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d650-f1"/> had officially stated in Baghdad that the Iraqi Minister
                    to Washington had reported that the latter had received assurances from this
                    Government that the United States desired, after the war, to see the
                    establishment of Arab states in Iraq, Palestine, and Transjordania.</p>
                <p>I assured Rabbi Wise that no such statements could possibly have been made
                    officially to the Iraqi Minister.</p>
                <p>Can you throw any light on this report? If not, I suggest that you take an early
                    opportunity of informing the Iraqi Minister that this report has come to my
                    attention and that, while I naturally assume there is no truth whatever in it, I
                    shall appreciate having any information he can give you about it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
